2026-10-10T13:00:26.4377065Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4387439Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4487494Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4497818Z [0m
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4498552Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4499277Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4499655Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4500257Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4501136Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4501679Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4502155Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4502870Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4503207Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4504064Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4505041Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4505569Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4505978Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4506154Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4506951Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4507276Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4507594Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4508040Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4508179Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4508313Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4508489Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4508891Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4509392Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4510779Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4510927Z I will:
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4511173Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4511398Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4511973Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4512803Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4513416Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4513696Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4514007Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4514767Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4515447Z    /root
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4528255Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4529202Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4541505Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4542480Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4546033Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4546587Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4548329Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4562678Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4563390Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4574179Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4575008Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4575846Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4576207Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4576527Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4577158Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4577702Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4578945Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4579399Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4579667Z If you would like to
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4580184Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4580500Z 
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4580857Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-10T13:00:26.4581487Z   $ sh ./install-nix
